## 2. English

### Full Caption (Instagram, YouTube Shorts, LinkedIn, Facebook)

```text
Today I pushed my Louisiana Bayou project forward and tackled a major compatibility hurdle.

I'm working with Unreal Engine 5.8 and Houdini 22, but no official plugin was available. So I compiled Adrian Pan's GitHub fork (Houdini Engine for Unreal) on Mac arm64, fully restoring the bridge.

Two approaches for HDA texturing:
1. Linking textures from disk into Content/HoudiniEngine/Temp: great for plug and play visual lookdev, but every HDA tweak costs around 3 seconds of cook time.
2. Referencing native materials already in the Unreal scene: Unreal only computes geometry, dropping cook time from 3s down to 0.3s. Speed is multiplied by ten!

To clearly distinguish both workflows in the viewport, I applied a blue color swap on the native material version. A great HDA balances designer comfort with smooth realtime performance. ᕙ(`▿´)ᕗ

Check out the last 10 seconds for the full 3D turntable showcase of the procedural church!

Portfolio & work: matthieuhuguet.com

